hi i mostly do reporting but i got asked to look at the caching and polling code for our internal dashboard (about 200 daily users) and i dont really know if its a good design. can you explain how the whole caching plus polling plus localstorage thing fits together and review the tradeoffs, like staleness, load on the api and what happens with many tabs open. no need to rewrite it i just want to understand if its a sensible approach

```js
const CACHE_KEY = 'dash_cache_v1';
let timer;

async function load(force) {
  const cached = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(CACHE_KEY) || 'null');
  if (cached && !force && Date.now() - cached.ts < 60000) return cached.data;
  const res = await fetch('/api/metrics?range=7d');
  const data = await res.json();
  localStorage.setItem(CACHE_KEY, JSON.stringify({ ts: Date.now(), data }));
  return data;
}

function startPolling(render) {
  timer = setInterval(async () => render(await load(true)), 15000);
}
```

